### `apply_patch`
The `apply_patch` tool can be used to edit files. This is a FREEFORM tool, so do not wrap the patch in JSON.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { apply_patch(input: string): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `exec_command`
Runs a command in a PTY, returning output or a session ID for ongoing interaction.

### Session shell helpers

These are shell commands on PATH. Use ordinary pipes. Options apply only to
commands whose usage lists them. Oversized output returns the first page with a
`session_id`; call `write_stdin` with that `session_id` and empty `chars` for
remaining pages, even after the command exits.

#### `mfinspect`

Outline source structure as START-END KIND NAME. Use `mfinspect [--json] PATH ...` before reading specific ranges. Output and errors are per file.

#### `mcat`

Read UTF-8 files or inclusive line ranges. Use `mcat [--number] PATH [START:END ...] ...`, e.g. `mcat src/main.rs 100:150`. Batch up to 16 reads. `-n N` limits rows in a single-file read; `--tail` selects the last rows and requires `-n`.

#### `msymbol`

Resolve definitions and references with `msymbol [--workspace ROOT] (def|refs) PATH [LINE] SYMBOL [N] ...`. Supply LINE for locals or ambiguous names; N chooses a token occurrence. Batch independent lookups. Rust analysis is offline and can report incomplete coverage.

#### `mrun`

Keep a bounded window from one foreground command: `mrun (-n N|--max-tokens N) [--head|--tail] [--] COMMAND [ARG...]`. The default is the tail. Data outside the window is discarded, not recoverable. Use native waits for background or interactive commands.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { exec_command(args: {
  // Shell command to execute.
  cmd: string;
  // User-facing approval question for `require_escalated`; omit otherwise.
  justification?: string;
  // Request login-shell startup. Omit to inherit.
  login?: boolean;
  // Output token budget. Defaults to 10000 tokens; larger requests may be capped by policy.
  max_output_tokens?: number;
  // Reusable approval prefix for `cmd`, only with `sandbox_permissions: "require_escalated"`; for example ["git", "pull"].
  prefix_rule?: Array<string>;
  // Per-command sandbox override. Defaults to `use_default`; use `require_escalated` for unsandboxed execution.
  sandbox_permissions?: "use_default" | "require_escalated";
  // Shell binary to launch. Defaults to the user's default shell.
  shell?: string;
  // True allocates a PTY for the command; false or omitted uses plain pipes.
  tty?: boolean;
  // Working directory for the command. Defaults to the turn cwd.
  workdir?: string;
  // Wait before yielding output. Defaults to 10000 ms; effective range is 250-30000 ms.
  yield_time_ms?: number;
}): Promise<{
  // Chunk identifier included when the response reports one.
  chunk_id?: string;
  // Process exit code when the command finished during this call.
  exit_code?: number;
  // Approximate token count before output truncation.
  original_token_count?: number;
  // Command output text for this page.
  output: string;
  // Session identifier to pass to write_stdin while running or while more output pages remain.
  session_id?: number;
  // Elapsed wall time spent waiting for output in seconds.
  wall_time_seconds: number;
}>; };
```

