### `write_stdin`
Writes characters to an existing unified exec session, or polls with empty chars for remaining output pages.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { write_stdin(args: {
  // Bytes to write to stdin. Defaults to empty, which polls or fetches the next output page without writing.
  chars?: string;
  // Output token budget. Defaults to 10000 tokens; larger requests may be capped by policy.
  max_output_tokens?: number;
  // Identifier of the unified exec session (running or with unread output pages).
  session_id: number;
  // Wait before yielding output. Non-empty writes default to 250 ms and cap at 30000 ms; empty polls wait 5000-300000 ms by default.
  yield_time_ms?: number;
}): Promise<{
  // Chunk identifier included when the response reports one.
  chunk_id?: string;
  // Process exit code when the command finished during this call.
  exit_code?: number;
  // Approximate token count before output truncation.
  original_token_count?: number;
  // Command output text for this page.
  output: string;
  // Session identifier to pass to write_stdin while running or while more output pages remain.
  session_id?: number;
  // Elapsed wall time spent waiting for output in seconds.
  wall_time_seconds: number;
}>; };
```

## clock
Tools for reading and waiting on time.

### `clock__curr_time`
Return the current time in UTC.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { clock__curr_time(args: {}): Promise<{
  // Current UTC time formatted as YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS UTC.
  current_time: string;
}>; };
```

## collaboration
Tools for spawning and managing sub-agents.

### `collaboration__followup_task`
Send a follow-up task to an existing non-root target agent and trigger a turn if it is idle. If the target is already running, deliver the task promptly at message boundaries while sampling, or after the pending tool call completes.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__followup_task(args: {
  // Message text to send to the target agent. Source references are read and frozen using the recipient's working directory and permissions.
  message: string;
  // Agent id or canonical task name to send a follow-up task to (from spawn_agent).
  target: string;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `collaboration__inspect_agent`
Inspect an agent's model, reasoning effort, service tier, context usage and completed compactions without loading it or starting work. Unavailable values are null.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__inspect_agent(args: {
  // Relative or canonical task name, or exact native thread ID.
  target: string;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `collaboration__interrupt_agent`
Interrupt an agent's current turn, if any, and return its previous status. The agent remains available for messages and follow-up tasks.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__interrupt_agent(args: {
  // Agent id or canonical task name to interrupt (from spawn_agent).
  target: string;
}): Promise<{
  // The agent status observed before the interrupt request was handled.
  previous_status: ("pending_init" | "running" | "interrupted" | "shutdown" | "not_found" | { completed: string | null; } | { errored: string; });
}>; };
```

### `collaboration__list_agents`
List live agents in the current root thread tree. Optionally filter by task-path prefix.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__list_agents(args: {
  // Relative or canonical task-path prefix without a trailing slash, or exact foreign agent ID to list its tree. Omit to list local live agents.
  path_prefix?: string;
}): Promise<{
  // Live agents visible in the current root thread tree.
  agents: Array<{
  // Canonical task name for the agent when available, otherwise the agent id.
  agent_name: string;
  // Last known status of the agent.
  agent_status: ("pending_init" | "running" | "interrupted" | "shutdown" | "not_found" | { completed: string | null; } | { errored: string; });
}>;
}>; };
```

### `collaboration__send_message`
Send a message to an existing agent. The message will be delivered promptly. Does not trigger a new turn.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__send_message(args: {
  // Ask in a fork of the loaded recipient's context with tools disabled, without steering its work. Defaults to false.
  btw?: boolean;
  // Message text to queue on the target agent, or a side question with btw=true. Source references are read and frozen using the recipient's working directory and permissions.
  message: string;
  // Relative or canonical task name to message (from spawn_agent). For another active session, use its exact thread ID.
  target: string;
}): Promise<unknown>; };
```

### `collaboration__spawn_agent`
Available model overrides (optional; inherited parent model is preferred):
- `gpt-6.2-sol`: Fast, go-to model for coding and everyday work. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6.2-astra`: Our most capable model for complex coding and professional work. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6.1-terra`: Efficient model that excels at visual understanding and computer use. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6.1-sol`: Previous generation model for coding and everyday work. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6-astra`: Previous generation model for complex coding and professional work. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6-sol`: Legacy model for coding and everyday work. Reasoning efforts: low, medium (default), high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-6-luna`: Fast and affordable model for easier tasks. Reasoning efforts: low, medium (default), high, xhigh, max. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-5.6-sol`: Legacy model for coding and everyday work. Reasoning efforts: low (default), medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-5.6-terra`: Legacy balanced model for agentic coding. Reasoning efforts: low, medium (default), high, xhigh, max, ultra. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-5.6-luna`: Legacy fast model for simpler tasks. Reasoning efforts: low, medium (default), high, xhigh, max. Service tiers: priority.
- `gpt-5.5`: Legacy coding model. Reasoning efforts: low, medium (default), high, xhigh. Service tiers: priority.
        Spawns an agent to work on the specified task. If your current task is `/root/task1` and you spawn_agent with task_name "task_3" the agent will have canonical task name `/root/task1/task_3`.
You are then able to refer to this agent as `task_3` or `/root/task1/task_3` interchangeably. However an agent `/root/task2/task_3` would only be able to communicate with this agent via its canonical name `/root/task1/task_3`.
The spawned agent will have the same tools as you and the ability to spawn its own subagents.

It will be able to send you and other running agents messages, and its final answer will be provided to you when it finishes.
The new agent's canonical task name will be provided to it along with the message.
For fork_turns=none, preload full applicable instructions/skills and needed owner evidence, not policy recaps; defer later-phase sources.

Note that passing `fork_turns="none"` will not pass any surrounding context to the spawned subagent, which may cause the agent to lack the context it needs to complete its task, whereas `fork_turns="all"` will provide the subagent with all surrounding context.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__spawn_agent(args: {
  // Child working directory. Omit to inherit yours; relative paths resolve from yours. Your working directory and permissions stay unchanged.
  cwd?: string;
  // Parent history to inherit. Defaults to `all`; use `none` to start without parent history. Only `all` and `none` are supported.
  fork_turns?: string;
  // Initial plain-text task for the new agent. Source references are read and frozen using the child's working directory and permissions.
  message: string;
  // Model override for the new agent. Omit unless an explicit override is needed.
  model?: string;
  // Sources to read before the child starts. Relative paths resolve from its working directory, and reads use its permissions. AGENTS.md is loaded automatically. Read failures are reported.
  preload?: {
  // Use @path for files, $skill for skills, or mchanges:ID for changes. Bare paths are invalid. Requires fork_turns: none.
  sources: Array<string>;
};
  // Reasoning effort override for the new agent. Omit to inherit the parent effort.
  reasoning_effort?: string;
  // Task name for the new agent. Use lowercase letters, digits, and underscores.
  task_name: string;
}): Promise<{
  // Canonical task name for the spawned agent.
  task_name: string;
}>; };
```

### `collaboration__wait_agent`
Wait for any (default) or all pending results from your descendant agents. Messages sent to you and new user input also end the wait. Omit yield_time_ms to wait without periodic progress updates; it is not a timeout. Final replies arrive as separate messages.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { collaboration__wait_agent(args: {
  // Wait until any (default) or all selected descendant agents finish, fail, or are interrupted.
  wait_mode?: "any" | "all";
  // Progress-update interval in milliseconds, minimum 300000. Omit to disable periodic updates. The interval starts summary collection; delivery waits for all requested summaries.
  yield_time_ms?: number;
}): Promise<{
  completed_agents: Array<string>;
  // Why the wait returned; agent replies arrive separately.
  message: string;
  // Combined changed-agent summaries and exact retained ranges, with bounded-output recovery when needed.
  progress: string;
}>; };
```

{
  "format": {
    "definition": "\nstart: pragma_source | plain_source\npragma_source: PRAGMA_LINE NEWLINE SOURCE\nplain_source: SOURCE\n\nPRAGMA_LINE: /[ \\t]*\\/\\/ @exec:[^\\r\\n]*/\nNEWLINE: /\\r?\\n/\nSOURCE: /[\\s\\S]+/\n",
    "syntax": "lark",
    "type": "grammar"
  },
  "name": "exec",
  "type": "custom"
}

# functions.wait
Waits on an `exec` cell or reads its next output page.
- Use `wait` with the cell ID when a response says the script is running or has more output.
  For a shell session ID, poll `tools.write_stdin` with empty `chars` instead.
- Reuse the same `cell_id` until the terminal response no longer says there is more output.

{
  "name": "wait",
  "parameters": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "cell_id": {
        "description": "Identifier of the exec cell.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "max_tokens": {
        "description": "Output token budget for this wait call. Defaults to 10000 tokens.",
        "type": "number"
      },
      "terminate": {
        "description": "True stops the running exec cell; false or omitted waits for output.",
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      "yield_time_ms": {
        "description": "Wait before yielding more output. Defaults to 10000 ms.",
        "type": "number"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "cell_id"
    ],
    "type": "object"
  },
  "strict": false,
  "type": "function"
}
